From: bbport
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: export the ICD entry points in the Android version script

An Android build exports only HMI (the hwvulkan HAL module). A process that dlopens the driver
directly calls vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr and vk_icdNegotiateLoaderICDInterfaceVersion, which
the driver contains but the version script made local.
---
diff --git a/src/vulkan/vulkan-android.sym b/src/vulkan/vulkan-android.sym
index 7148e09..3f97261 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/vulkan-android.sym
+++ b/src/vulkan/vulkan-android.sym
@@ -5,6 +5,12 @@
 		# instance of struct hwvulkan_module_t.
 		HMI;
 
+		# The ICD entry points too: a process that dlopens the driver directly (no hwvulkan
+		# loader in between) reaches the driver through these.
+		vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr;
+		vk_icdGetPhysicalDeviceProcAddr;
+		vk_icdNegotiateLoaderICDInterfaceVersion;
+
 	local:
 		# When static linking LLVM, all its symbols are public API.
 		# That may cause symbol collision, so explicitly demote everything.
